## Definitions

The **licensor** is the individual or entity offering these
terms, and the **software** is the software the licensor
makes available under these terms.

**You** refers to the individual or entity agreeing to these
terms.

**Your company** is any legal entity, sole proprietorship,
or other kind of organization that you work for, plus all
its affiliates that control it, are under its control,
or are under common control with it.

**Affiliates** means the other entities that control a
party, are controlled by a party, or are under common
control with that party.  **Control** means ownership of
substantially all the assets or power to direct management
of an entity.

**To compete** with the licensor means to develop,
manufacture, distribute, or provide a product or service
that is offered to the same or similar market as the
software (or any product or service of the licensor that
the software adds value to).
